# Command line interface

`main.go` owns flag parsing, input selection, and output. `run` takes its arguments and streams explicitly so tests drive it without a subprocess.

Output is a public contract that scripts parse: one line per input with the selected columns in the fixed order lines, words, bytes, each right-aligned in eight characters, then a space and the input name. Standard input has no name. A `total` line follows when more than one file is given. Change the format only with the owner's agreement.

Errors go to standard error prefixed `tally:`. A failing file sets exit status 1 but does not stop the remaining inputs; flag errors exit with status 2.
